# Bebop & Rocksteady attack with no card in their controller's hand: the discard cannot be paid (CR 118.12a), so no
# choice to discard is offered and a permanent is sacrificed. Bot1 empties its hand on turn 1 (Sol Ring, two Moxen and
# two Ornithopters cast, then Bebop & Rocksteady), plays the turn-3 draw, and attacks; it sacrifices an Ornithopter.
# The discard prompt the other scenarios answer is the positive control for the refusal.

[Bot1 Deck]
Swamp
Sol Ring
Mox Jet
Mox Emerald
Bebop & Rocksteady
Ornithopter
Ornithopter
Swamp x12

[Bot2 Deck]
Island x20

[Actions]
Bot1.Hand.Swamp.Play
Bot1.Battlefield.Swamp.Activate
Bot1.Hand.Sol Ring.Cast
Bot1.Hand.Mox Jet.Cast
Bot1.Hand.Mox Emerald.Cast
Bot1.Hand.Ornithopter.Cast
Bot1.Hand.Ornithopter.Cast
Bot1.Battlefield.Sol Ring.Activate
Bot1.Battlefield.Mox Jet.Activate
Bot1.Battlefield.Mox Emerald.Activate
Bot1.Hand.Bebop & Rocksteady.Cast
[T3 Bot1.Main1]
Bot1.Hand.Swamp.Play
[T3 Bot1.DeclareAttackers]
Bot1.Attack(Bebop & Rocksteady)
! Bot1.Decline
Bot1.Choose(Ornithopter)
[T3 Bot1.Main2]

[Expect]
Bot1.Hand.Count = 0
Bot1.Graveyard = Ornithopter
Bot1.Battlefield.Bebop & Rocksteady.Tapped = true
Bot2.Life = 13
